Here is the root cause:
The bug occurs because the initial wakeup interrupt triggered by the extcon event only brings the controller out of low power mode without handling any subsequent events. This results in the extcon use case not functioning correctly after the controller resumes, as it fails to process necessary events that may have occurred during the low power state.

